cert.h is generated with the following command,
python cert.py -s api.openweathermap.org,api.open-meteo.com,api.weather.gov -p 443 -n providers > cert.h

The NOAA provider uses the `api.weather.gov` chain when `HTTPS_VERIFY` is
selected. Keep the existing certificate symbols when regenerating the file;
all verified providers include their own trusted chain.

MeteoSwiss uses the ESP-IDF full certificate bundle instead of pinning its
rotating `*.meteoswiss-app.ch` leaf certificate. The current App endpoint is
served by Amazon RSA 2048 M01; the bundled Amazon Root CA 1 validates that
chain. Keep `CONFIG_MBEDTLS_CERTIFICATE_BUNDLE_DEFAULT_FULL=y` enabled for
verified MeteoSwiss builds.
